614
00:34:35,180 --> 00:34:40,060
但真正让人惊讶的是，这花了我
But what is genuinely staggering
is this cost me

615
00:34:40,060 --> 00:34:42,260
一万四千便士。
14,000 pence.

616
00:34:42,260 --> 00:34:43,340
是啊……
Yes...

617
00:34:43,380 --> 00:34:47,380
一块 Vauxhall Frontera 的更换离合器大概要
A replacement clutch for
a Vauxhall Frontera is around about

618
00:34:47,380 --> 00:34:52,580
300到400。于是我这儿找到了半价离合器
300- 400. So I have got here
a half-price clutch

619
00:34:52,620 --> 00:34:57,460
还顺带送了一整辆车，免费且已通过MOT检查、已交税。
with an entire car thrown in
for free and MOT'd and taxed.

620
00:34:57,500 --> 00:35:00,500
是啊，不过，那整辆车就是 Vauxhall Frontera。
Yeah, but, the entire car is
a Vauxhall Frontera.

621
00:35:00,500 --> 00:35:02,180
是啊，你最后剩下的是……
Yeah, you are left with a...

622
00:35:02,180 --> 00:35:06,700
什么？听着，花掉140镑，我也不在乎格栅上写着“狗屎”。
What? Look, for 140 quid, I wouldn't
care if it said "dog dirt"
on the grille.

623
00:35:06,700 --> 00:35:08,740
基本就是这么回事。
It pretty much does.

624
00:35:08,780 --> 00:35:10,340
再看看那家伙……看后面。
And look what the chap...
Look in the back.

625
00:35:10,340 --> 00:35:12,860
哦，一个向外摆的门，这样你根本打不开它进超市
Oh, a swing-away door so you can't
open it in a supermarket

626
00:35:12,860 --> 00:35:15,420
或者它是……哦，我的天……！
or it's... Oh, my G...!

627
00:35:15,420 --> 00:35:17,020
你的狗会有多开心？
How happy would your dog be?

628
00:35:17,020 --> 00:35:19,700
我只听到一个词——“受害者”。
All I can hear is the word "victim".

629
00:35:19,740 --> 00:35:23,340
这可不是杀人凶器的车。那是给你的悬挂滑翔机的。
They're not murderers' cars.
That's for your hang glider.

630
00:35:23,380 --> 00:35:29,260
‘迫不及待想试试我们这超便宜的机器，于是上路了。’
'Eager to test our incredibly
cheap machines, we hit the road.'

631
00:35:39,980 --> 00:35:44,260
虽然这只花了140，
Even though this was only 140,

632
00:35:44,260 --> 00:35:49,220
前车主免费附送了这些空气清新剂，
the previous owner has thrown in,
for free, these air fresheners,

633
00:35:49,260 --> 00:35:52,380
让车厢里弥漫着一股热腾腾的……
which give the cabin
the aroma of a hot...

634
00:35:52,420 --> 00:35:53,980
土耳其小便池的味道。
Turkish urinal.

635
00:35:55,100 --> 00:35:56,420
还有更多。
And there's more.

636
00:35:56,420 --> 00:35:59,060
在中间的小格子里，我发现他给我留了
In the centre cubby hole,
I find he's left me

637
00:35:59,100 --> 00:36:01,100
一副他旧的太阳镜。
a pair of his old sunglasses.

638
00:36:01,140 --> 00:36:05,180
还有……这些耳机，里面沾有
And...these earphones,
which come with traces

639
00:36:05,180 --> 00:36:09,020
他个人专属的耳垢痕迹。
of his personalised earwax.

640
00:36:09,020 --> 00:36:10,780
简直不可思议。
Unbelievable.

641
00:36:10,820 --> 00:36:15,220
而且这些全部都是在标配之外的额外配置。
And all of this is in addition
to what comes as standard.

642
00:36:15,220 --> 00:36:19,180
空调正常运作，电动窗户，安全气囊，
Functioning air conditioning,
electric windows, air bags,

643
00:36:19,220 --> 00:36:22,620
电动后视镜，双天窗。
electric door mirrors,
two sunshine roofs.

644
00:36:23,900 --> 00:36:27,700
而且性价比还不止于此。
'And the value for money
doesn't stop there.'

645
00:36:27,700 --> 00:36:30,780
这车的残值大概，咱说两百英镑左右。
The scrap value of this car is
about, let's say 200 quid.

646
00:36:30,820 --> 00:36:35,660
所以，要是我撞了它，反而还能多省六十英镑。
So, if I crash it,
I'll be 60 quid better off.

647
00:36:36,860 --> 00:36:39,220
出个车祸还能赚钱呢。
I can make money by having
an accident.

648
00:36:45,980 --> 00:36:50,260
说实话，我对整个项目抱着极度怀疑的态度。
I'll be honest, I was deeply cynical
of this whole enterprise.

649
00:36:50,260 --> 00:36:55,380
我直接站起来回嘴：“没门，二百五的四驱车根本买不到。”
I just stood up and said, "No way,
you can't buy 4x4s for 250 quid."

650
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:57,340
然而，它竟然真的在这儿。
And yet, here it is.

651
00:36:58,340 --> 00:36:59,700
它不是完美的。
It's not perfect.

652
00:36:59,740 --> 00:37:04,700
后视镜……根本没有。头枕也没了。
Rear view mirror is...not there.
Head rests have gone.

653
00:37:04,700 --> 00:37:08,940
除此之外，还有空调，超赞的立体声系统，
Other than that, there's air
conditioning, very nice stereo,

654
00:37:08,980 --> 00:37:12,380
六碟多碟机，磁带播放器——历史感十足。
six-CD multichanger, cassette
player - nice touch of history.

655
00:37:12,380 --> 00:37:13,900
扬声器堆得满满的。
Loads of speakers.

656
00:37:15,260 --> 00:37:16,940
简直太棒了。
It's brilliant.

657
00:37:16,940 --> 00:37:18,300
我有木头。
I've got wood.

658
00:37:18,340 --> 00:37:19,940
就在这。
There.

659
00:37:24,780 --> 00:37:27,340
这车刚上市时，我其实写过一篇评测。
I actually wrote a review of this
car when it was new.

660
00:37:27,340 --> 00:37:31,140
我记得它的越野性能让我印象深刻。
And I remember being very impressed
at how good it was off-road.

661
00:37:31,180 --> 00:37:34,740
它配备了正经的分动箱，高低速两档，
This has a proper transfer box,
high and low range,

662
00:37:34,740 --> 00:37:36,380
还有差速锁。
and differential locks.

663
00:37:36,420 --> 00:37:40,540
排量只有1.8升，但动力相当灵活。
It's only 1.8 litres,
but it is quite spritely.

664
00:37:40,540 --> 00:37:44,820
而且车身很轻，比另外两款轻了差不多四百公斤。
And it's very light.
It's almost 400 kilograms lighter
than the other two.

665
00:37:44,820 --> 00:37:48,180
不过，事儿也不是全好。
Mind you, it wasn't all good news.

666
00:37:48,220 --> 00:37:53,020
前车主确实提醒过我，其中一个刹车碟“略微变形”。
The previous owner did warn me that
one of the brake discs was
"slightly warped".

667
00:37:54,460 --> 00:37:56,620
他没说的其实是，它，呃，
What he didn't actually say
was that it's, well,

668
00:37:56,660 --> 00:37:58,340
看起来像是被折成了直角。
it appears to be bent
at right angles.

669
00:37:58,340 --> 00:38:00,660
刹车时……RATTLING
When you brake...
RATTLING

670
00:38:00,660 --> 00:38:02,380
..抖动得惊人。
..the juddering is appalling.

671
00:38:02,420 --> 00:38:03,900
真的一点儿都不…
It really doesn't...

672
00:38:03,940 --> 00:38:05,620
妈呀，天呐！
Cor, blimey!

673
00:38:09,140 --> 00:38:14,180
我们很快抵达了Top Gear的绝密生活方式测试跑道…
'Soon we arrived at Top Gear's
top secret lifestyle test track...

674
00:38:14,220 --> 00:38:18,260
它就在Ladyhole Lane旁边，向西大约一英里
'which is just off Ladyhole Lane,
one mile to the west

675
00:38:18,300 --> 00:38:20,060
离Ellastone村庄不远。
'of the village of Ellastone.

676
00:38:21,100 --> 00:38:23,700
在这座最尖端的设施里，
'At this state-of-the-art facility,

677
00:38:23,700 --> 00:38:26,540
我们首先冲进了室内冬季测试中心，
'we headed first
to the indoor winter testing centre,

678
00:38:26,540 --> 00:38:31,900
在那里我们发现，呃，这些车在坡道上根本不怎么行。
'where we discovered our cars
weren't much good on the, um,
inclines.'

679
00:38:31,940 --> 00:38:34,060
上坡，上坡！
Up, up the hill!

680
00:38:34,060 --> 00:38:35,220
CLANKING
CLANKING

681
00:38:35,260 --> 00:38:37,820
我正想把它挂到四驱。
I'm trying to put it
in four-wheel drive.

682
00:38:39,020 --> 00:38:41,780
哦，不！出问题了。
Oh, no! Something's gone wrong.

683
00:38:42,940 --> 00:38:46,140
拜托，别这样！你怎么倒着走？
Come on, no!
Why are you going backwards?

684
00:38:46,180 --> 00:38:47,660
我不行……
I can't...

685
00:38:47,700 --> 00:38:48,940
哎呀！
Ugh!

686
00:38:50,300 --> 00:38:51,340
胡扯。
Bollocks.

687
00:38:51,340 --> 00:38:52,540
我搞不定……
I can't get it...

688
00:38:53,940 --> 00:38:55,380
杰里米笑
JEREMY LAUGHS

689
00:38:56,820 --> 00:39:00,060
‘我们随后被告知去椭圆测试跑道，’
'We were then told to report
to the oval test track,

690
00:39:00,100 --> 00:39:02,620
‘在那里我们接到挑战。’
'where we received a challenge.'

691
00:39:02,620 --> 00:39:04,740
这是一场捉人游戏。
It's a game of tag.

692
00:39:04,740 --> 00:39:09,420
‘你们每个人在绝密椭圆测试跑道上有不同的起点。
"You each have a different start
point on the top secret oval
test track.

693
00:39:09,420 --> 00:39:11,140
‘而且你们同时出发。
"And you each begin at once.

694
00:39:11,180 --> 00:39:14,500
‘目标是不被超越，若被超车，你就出局。
"The object is not to be overtaken.
If you are, you're out.

695
00:39:14,500 --> 00:39:19,220
‘为了让测试更贴近实际，你们每人会有一个配重。
"And to make the test more relevant,
you will each have a ballast."

696
00:39:19,220 --> 00:39:22,020
配重？字幕上就是这么写的，‘配重’。
A ballast?
That's what it says, "a ballast".

697
00:39:25,300 --> 00:39:27,820
对，这就是那个‘配重’。是啊。
Right, this is the "a ballast".
Yeah.

698
00:39:27,860 --> 00:39:29,180
其实这很有关联。
And actually it is relevant.

699
00:39:29,220 --> 00:39:30,340
是吗？没错，就是这样。
Is it? No, it is.

700
00:39:30,340 --> 00:39:34,420
因为SUV车主的‘休闲活动’之一
Because one of the "leisure
activities" done by SUV people

701
00:39:34,420 --> 00:39:37,060
就是去泥泞的田野度假。
is going on holiday in
a muddy field.

702
00:39:37,100 --> 00:39:40,900
是的。不相关的是我的拖车大小。
Yes. What isn't relevant is
the size of my caravan.

703
00:39:40,940 --> 00:39:42,820
什么情况？为什么给我
What do you mean?
Why have I been given

704
00:39:42,820 --> 00:39:44,740
这么巨大的……？看看它的尺寸。
such an enormous...?
Look at the size of it.

705
00:39:44,780 --> 00:39:47,420
不不，拖车不大。你的车才小。
No, no, the caravan
isn't big. Your car is small.

706
00:39:47,460 --> 00:39:49,260
他……他说得对。
He...he's right.

707
00:39:51,860 --> 00:39:56,860
‘最终，我们停止争吵，走到跑道上各自占位，’
'Eventually, we stopped
bickering and took our start
positions on the track,

708
00:39:56,900 --> 00:40:00,780
‘结果发现有个意外的后期参赛者。’
'where it turned out
there was a surprise late entry.'

709
00:40:02,580 --> 00:40:04,140
我清楚知道那是谁。
I know exactly who it is.

710
00:40:04,140 --> 00:40:07,500
各位先生女士，那并不是斯提格。
That, ladies and gentlemen,
is not the Stig.

711
00:40:07,500 --> 00:40:11,100
那是《Top Gear》最高机密的休闲斯提格。
That is Top Gear's top secret
Leisure Stig.

712
00:40:11,100 --> 00:40:11,980
废物司机。
Useless driver.

713
00:40:13,260 --> 00:40:16,020
我们只用他来测试拖车。
We use him only for
testing caravans.

714
00:40:17,620 --> 00:40:20,900
坦诺伊：三、二、一，开始！
TANNOY: Three, two, one, go!

715
00:40:24,340 --> 00:40:25,660
开始啦。
Here we go.

716
00:40:25,660 --> 00:40:28,460
测试，测试已经开始。
Testing, testing has begun.

717
00:40:28,500 --> 00:40:35,260
我现在让这台134马力的Vauxhall Vectra发动机狂飙。
I'm now unleashing the 134
horsepower Vauxhall Vectra engine.

718
00:40:35,300 --> 00:40:39,300
‘可悲的是，休闲斯提格的驾驶太慢，
'Sadly, though,
Leisure Stig's driving was so slow,

719
00:40:39,340 --> 00:40:42,220
‘于是他很快就造成了点小堵车。’
'that soon he was causing
a bit of a traffic jam.'

720
00:40:42,260 --> 00:40:43,460
哦！
Oh!

721
00:40:43,460 --> 00:40:48,180
他们怎么会给我这么巨大的拖车？真是无望啊。
Why have they given me such
a massive caravan? This is hopeless.

722
00:40:48,220 --> 00:40:50,020
“嗯，还能更糟。”
'Well, it could be worse.'

723
00:40:50,060 --> 00:40:53,420
我能感觉到我那个“配重”产生的下压力，还不错。
I can feel the downforce
from my "a ballast", and it's good.

724
00:40:53,420 --> 00:40:56,260
哎呀！我搞砸了。
Ohh! I've gone wrong.

725
00:40:56,260 --> 00:40:59,100
真是无望，我撞到自己了。
It's hopeless. I've crashed into
myself.

726
00:41:00,100 --> 00:41:02,580
别被超过去，否则我就寄了。
I mustn't be overtaken or I'm out.

727
00:41:02,580 --> 00:41:07,940
“凭借强大的Frontera，我追上了哈蒙德
'Using the power of the mighty
Frontera, I caught up with Hammond

728
00:41:07,940 --> 00:41:10,860
并试图在内线抢位……”
'and tried to take him on
the inside...

729
00:41:10,900 --> 00:41:14,140
“这意味着要冲上那块专门用来考验悬挂的路面。”
'which meant going onto the surface
designed to test suspension.'

730
00:41:15,620 --> 00:41:18,620
哦，这段更糟糕！
Oh, this bit's even worse!

731
00:41:22,780 --> 00:41:27,740
全场乱套，我在那儿抢到的优势全毁了。
Total chaos, and I've lost
all the ground I made up there.

732
00:41:29,180 --> 00:41:34,340
“因为休闲版斯提格太慢，连詹姆斯都开始不耐烦了。”
'Because Leisure Stig was so slow,
even James was getting impatient.'

733
00:41:34,380 --> 00:41:37,580
抖得要命，气流冲击。加油，Pinin！
Juddering, buffeting.
Come on, Pinin!

734
00:41:37,580 --> 00:41:39,500
“而且还挺激进的。”
'And violent.'

735
00:41:43,420 --> 00:41:46,220
哦，好戏。他车轮都快掉了。
Oh, yes. He's losing the wheel.

736
00:41:46,260 --> 00:41:48,260
斯提格犯了大错误。
Massive error by the Stig.

737
00:41:48,300 --> 00:41:51,500
烟雾滚滚而出。
Smoke is pouring off.

738
00:41:53,020 --> 00:41:54,980
好，这次哈蒙德，你完蛋了！
Right, this time, Hammond,
you're going down!

739
00:41:56,420 --> 00:41:57,420
噢！
Oh!

740
00:42:00,660 --> 00:42:02,380
糟了！
Oh, no!

741
00:42:08,740 --> 00:42:11,180
“于是哈蒙德出错了。”
'Then Hammond made an error.'

742
00:42:11,180 --> 00:42:12,620
我在那段凹凸路面上。
I'm on the rough stuff.

743
00:42:12,660 --> 00:42:15,500
哦，这简直……
Oh, this is impossibly...

744
00:42:15,500 --> 00:42:20,980
哦，哦。抱歉哈蒙德，我们已经超过去了，你完蛋了。
Oh, yeah. I'm sorry, Hammond.
We have overtaken you. You are out.

745
00:42:23,820 --> 00:42:25,820
我想我现在掉轮了。
I think I've lost a wheel now.

746
00:42:25,820 --> 00:42:27,660
火花四溅。
Lot of sparks.

747
00:42:27,660 --> 00:42:30,500
说实话，这车几乎控制不住……
It's...it's barely controllable,
if I'm honest.

748
00:42:40,140 --> 00:42:43,700
哦，我现在，终于看出问题所在了。
Oh, now I, I can see the problem
here.

749
00:42:43,740 --> 00:42:47,140
“与此同时，我的比赛进行得顺利。”
'Meanwhile, my race was going well.'

750
00:42:47,140 --> 00:42:50,780
是的，我刚超了詹姆斯·梅。他莫名其妙地被甩到了内场。
Yes, I've just done James May.
He's somehow ended up on the
infield.

751
00:42:52,420 --> 00:42:55,300
那是一次灾难性的失误。
That was a catastrophic mistake.

752
00:42:55,300 --> 00:42:59,540
“可惜，我在想抢到休闲版斯提格时把局面搞得太烂了。”
'But sadly, I overcooked it
trying to take Leisure Stig.'

753
00:43:01,580 --> 00:43:02,580
啊——！
Aaargh!

754
00:43:05,260 --> 00:43:08,300
哦！刹车全失灵了。
Oh! Lost my brakes completely.

755
00:43:11,660 --> 00:43:16,140
“跑完20圈后，休闲版斯提格已经放弃了。”
'With 20 laps completed,
Leisure Stig had given up.

756
00:43:16,180 --> 00:43:19,140
“哈蒙德仍以为自己还在赛场上……”
'Hammond still thought
he was in the contest...

757
00:43:19,140 --> 00:43:20,980
“而我已经出大问题了。”
'and I had a problem.'

758
00:43:21,020 --> 00:43:25,140
Frontera前部冒出蒸汽。
Steam coming from the front
of the Frontera.

759
00:43:25,140 --> 00:43:27,580
Vauxhall这边情况不妙。
Things are not good in the Vauxhall.

760
00:43:27,580 --> 00:43:31,100
好啊，来了，我可以把他碾过去。加油！
Yes, here we go, I can have him.
Come on!

761
00:43:31,140 --> 00:43:34,900
哎呀！后面太紧了，紧得要命。
Uh-oh! It's tight, it's tight
at the back.

762
00:43:36,380 --> 00:43:39,780
操控尝试来自
杰里米·克拉克森。
Manoeuvre attempt by
Jeremy Clarkson.

763
00:43:39,820 --> 00:43:41,500
啊——！
Argh!

764
00:43:41,500 --> 00:43:43,620
啊！啊！
Ah! Ah!

765
00:43:48,140 --> 00:43:51,340
他上了坡顶。
喇叭响
He's up the bank.
TOOTS HORN

766
00:43:52,380 --> 00:43:55,260
我觉得我们有点忘了这场比赛的规则。
I think we might have lost sight
of the rules of this race slightly.

767
